  "method": "fetch.py requests one zip per survey year and quarter from the DATRAS Download API (50 files, 13.6 MB) and records their checksums. analysis.py pools all records, converts length classes to cm, drops plus-group and unaged records, and computes the CANoAtLngt-weighted mean length at age per species. For the 11 species with at least 7 consecutive age classes from age 1 each holding >= 50 aged fish, it fits by weighted least squares a 3-parameter von Bertalanffy curve and a 3-parameter quadratic-plateau curve whose maximum is reached at least one age class before the oldest included age, and compares them by AIC; it also records the sign of the three increments between the last four included age classes.",
